<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Mine inspectors strike Australia's NSW state.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Mine inspectors strike Australia's NSW state.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>New South Wales mine inspectors walked off the job for 48 hours from midnight (1300 GMT) on Wednesday in protest over pay claims and failure to fill vacancies across the state.</p>
<p>The inspectors claimed in a statement the safety of mine workers in New South Wales is at risk as a result of a failure by the Department of Minerals to recruit suitably qualified staff to fill job openings.</p>
<p>A spokesman for the Department of Minerals said mine production would not be affected by the strike as ultimately it was up to operators to provide for safety at mines.  </p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
